workedExamples.question_text:
Seven friends, including Ava and Ben, stand in a uniformly random order in a row. Find the probability that:
(a) Ava and Ben stand together;
(b) Ava and Ben do not stand together.

workedExamples.solution_text:
Fix Noor's position. Eli has nine equally likely remaining seats, exactly one of which is opposite Noor.
The diagram marks Noor's fixed seat and the required seat for Eli; the other seats can be filled in any order.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1mm,y=1mm]
\draw[draw=black] (0,0) circle (14);
\foreach \a in {18,54,126,162,198,234,306,342} {
\draw[draw=black,fill=white] (\a:19) circle (1.3);
}
\draw[draw=black,fill=white] (90:19) circle (1.3);
\draw[draw=black,fill=white] (270:19) circle (1.3);
\path (0,24) node[text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont] {Noor};
\path (0,-24) node[text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont] {Eli};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$P(\text{opposite})=\frac{1}{9}$.
